I think it is accurate to say that the designation of 'open system' no matter
what the topic is, cannot be made without reference to: (1) a space scale, (2) a
time scale, and most important as far as humans are concerned, (3) a
technological scale of our ability to focus and control the flow of energy (read
as applied knowledge of objective reality - information content within
space-time).  Call this a General Theory of Relativity of Open Systems.

I think those who speculate about the universe as a whole being a
thermodynamically closed system are members of a secret neo-Gnostic cult of
entropic death-worshippers.

